WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.932
Now we combine the ideas into one small cleaning workflow.

00:00:03.932 --> 00:00:11.797
The raw sales extract contains inconsistent text, a currency-formatted amount, an invalid date, missing values,

00:00:11.797 --> 00:00:13.287
and a duplicated order.

00:00:13.287 --> 00:00:20.397
The workflow removes the duplicate, standardizes channel and status text, removes the currency symbol,

00:00:20.397 --> 00:00:27.062
converts amount to numeric, converts order date to a date-time type, fills the missing city,

00:00:27.062 --> 00:00:31.269
and fills the missing amount using the median.

00:00:31.746 --> 00:00:33.953
The important lesson is the sequence.

00:00:33.953 --> 00:00:36.988
We are not collecting random cleaning functions.

00:00:36.988 --> 00:00:42.248
We are moving from raw data toward a table with consistent types and categories.

00:00:42.248 --> 00:00:47.386
Each transformation should solve a specific problem that we previously identified.
